
Grab all symbiont TransDecoder protein sequences that matched K04564, this is
transcript_symb.faa

Use the following to generate tmp/sequences.faa, which we renamed to
transcript_symb_multiM.faa

PYTHONPATH=../coral sieve-py ../sieve/scripts/filter-fasta-by-rules.py \
  --fasta transcript_symb.faa \
  -r coral.rules.MnFeSOD_algae_discovery.rule_fasta \
  --artifacts-dir tmp \
  --pfam-hmm assets/pfam.hmm \
  --ko-hmm assets/k04564.hmm \
  --ko-thresholds assets/k04564_threshold.tsv --sequences-only

transcript_symb_multiM.faa was submitted to DeepLoc 2.1, results downloaded as
transcript_symb_multiM.deeploc.csv. Also, keep the job ID for DeepLoc as we
will be looking at the visual results as well.

Use the following to filter transcript_symb.faa through residue rules

PYTHONPATH=../coral sieve-py ../sieve/scripts/filter-fasta-by-rules.py \
  --fasta transcript_symb.faa \
  -r coral.rules.MnFeSOD_algae_discovery.rule_fasta \
  --artifacts-dir tmp \
  --pfam-hmm assets/pfam.hmm \
  --ko-hmm assets/k04564.hmm \
  --ko-thresholds assets/k04564_threshold.tsv --deeploc-csv transcript_symb_multiM.deeploc.csv

Removing sequences that did not pass residue / domain match rules, we are left
with sequences in transcript_symb_multiM_residue.faa, which also only includes
a longer protein sequence if that passed and removed the truncated versions of
that protein sequence.

Using DeepLoc results for sequences in transcript_symb_multiM_residue.faa, we
generated transcript_symb_residue_forwarded.faa to include additional
truncations that start at a trough in the SP attention reported by DeepLoc.  We
then re-queried DeepLoc with these new truncations. DeepLoc reported Golgi and
Extracellular for the non-truncated proteins, and for the truncated proteins,
which were all truncations of the Galgi-called proteins, DeepLoc reported
Plastid. This further supports a tandom SP-cTP architecture in the leader
sequence.
